A multi-line `--asked` is whitespace-normalised to one line, so it cannot open a heading or break
the entry.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
macro_stubs:
  "core.macros.date +%Y-%m-%d %H:%M": "2026-10-15 16:40"
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p/index.md --
---
title: P
---

# P
-- cmd --
sh -c 'booping defaults add --target plans/p/index.md --step groom/present --asked "$(printf "Approve the plan?\n## Not a heading")" --default "approved"'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/p/defaults.md#D1
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/vault/plans/p/defaults.md --
# Defaults

## D1 — groom/present — 2026-10-15 16:40

**Asked:** Approve the plan? ## Not a heading

**Default:** approved

**Why:** not stated

**Artifact:** [index.md](index.md)
